# honey-starter - Environment Variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` at the repo root and adjust as needed. The repo-root
# `.env` is sourced by `scripts/start.sh` (via scripts/lib.sh) on every run. When
# you invoke `docker compose -f deploy/docker-compose.yaml` directly, export the
# variables in your shell or set them in `deploy/.env` (compose loads `.env`
# from the compose file's directory). The Makefile validation gates set their
# own safe defaults and do not read the repo `.env`.
#
# NOTE: the guided writer for this file is `scripts/setup.sh` (run
# `bash scripts/setup.sh --help`). It generates/rewrites .env with a
# questionnaire, preserves unmanaged lines byte-exact, manages the HONEY_NS /
# HONEY_USER / HD_AI_* / HD_*_HOST_PORT keys, and replaces the AI secret keys
# only on an explicit value. Hand-editing below still works and is preserved.
#
# Environment namespaces (see deploy/README.md):
#   * HD_*              template-fed daemon settings: the config loader exposes
#                       env vars prefixed HD_ to `{% .env.X %}` templates with
#                       the prefix stripped (HD_UI_URL -> .env.UI_URL).
#   * plain env         consumed directly by processes, NOT visible to config
#                       templates: REPO, BRANCH, CHECK_REMOTE, LOCALREDIS,
#                       VAULT_ADDR, VAULT_ROLE_ID, VAULT_SECRET_ID,
#                       HD_SECURE_LOADER, HD_JWT_SIGNING_KEY, HOME, plus the
#                       start.sh provisioning knobs (HONEY_NS, HONEY_USER, ...).
#   * hd-secret-file:// compose env values are materialized by the daemon image
#                       entrypoint from /var/hd-secrets/<name> before exec.
#
# Operational secrets are NEVER set here. Secrets (admin token hash, AI API
# keys, ...) live in Vault under secrets/data/<ns>/daemon and are resolved by
# the daemon at config-load time via LOOKUP[vault,...]. The only secret outside
# Vault is the AppRole identity pair used to reach Vault, written by start.sh
# into .honey-starter/identity/ and mounted into the daemon read-only.
#
# NOTE: integration toggles (GitHub/Slack/Kubernetes) are configured
# statically in bootstrap/init.yaml, not here.

# --- Deployment (docker compose) ---
# Absolute path to the generated runtime state directory (rendered config,
# AppRole identity files, root token/unseal key, admin token). Leave unset for
# the default <repo>/.honey-starter. If you set it, use an ABSOLUTE path:
# compose anchors relative paths at deploy/, not the repo root.
# HD_STATE_DIR=

# Host published ports (override on the docker host).
# HD_API_HOST_PORT=9000
# HD_UI_HOST_PORT=8090

# Public base URL of the Honeydipper UI (used for OAuth/SAML redirect building;
# inert with auth-simple token auth). Fed to the daemon template .env.UI_URL.
# HD_UI_URL=http://localhost:8090

# Daemon API container port. Also feeds the listener template .env.API_PORT.
# HD_API_PORT=9000

# Config watch/reload interval. Feeds template .env.CONFIG_CHECK_INTERVAL.
# Defaults to 30m in the compose deployment (deliberate tradeoff — see
# deploy/README.md "Config reload behavior": each tick re-resolves every Vault
# LOOKUP with a fresh AppRole login, and while Vault is down a reload storm
# flaps /healthz). Lower it only if you accept that churn, or once upstream
# gains fsnotify-backed reloads.
# HD_CONFIG_CHECK_INTERVAL=30m

# Container images. Override to pin or test a different build.
# HONEYDIPPER_IMAGE=honeydipper/honeydipper:4.0.0-alpha4-53-g897242b
# VALKEY_IMAGE=valkey/valkey:8.1.0
# VAULT_IMAGE=hashicorp/vault:1.21.1
# HD_UI_IMAGE=honeydipper/hd-ui:0.1.0-alpha2-52-g0ea2fad

# --- start.sh provisioning knobs ---
# Vault KV namespace prefix baked into the rendered config and the Vault seed
# paths (secrets/data/<ns>/daemon). MUST be a single Vault path segment
# ([A-Za-z0-9._-]) and MUST stay constant for the life of a deployment —
# start.sh refuses to proceed if it changes after the first run. Leave unset
# for the default "starter".
# HONEY_NS=starter

# Admin subject bound to the casbin `editor` role. The bearer token start.sh
# prints on first run maps to this subject. MUST stay constant after first run.
# Leave unset for the default "admin".
# HONEY_USER=admin

# Vault unseal key shares / threshold. start.sh initializes Vault on first run
# with these values and persists every key to .honey-starter/unseal_key
# (chmod 600). For a starter deployment 1/1 is convenient; increase (e.g. 5/3)
# for higher-assurance hosts and back up the extra keys yourself. Once Vault
# is initialized these values are inert (start.sh detects and unseals with the
# persisted keys).
# HONEY_VAULT_KEY_SHARES=1
# HONEY_VAULT_KEY_THRESHOLD=1

# --- AI provider (start.sh) ---
# AI API keys are NEVER stored in compose/.env as operational secrets: they are
# seeded into Vault at secrets/data/<ns>/daemon by start.sh on first run, and
# the daemon reads them from Vault via LOOKUP at config-load time. Set them in
# your shell or in this .env ONLY as provisioning inputs (start.sh reads the
# value once and writes it into Vault). Leave unset to store a clearly-marked
# placeholder; export the real key and re-run `make start` to replace it.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Non-secret AI routing knobs. In the compose deployment these are wired into
# the daemon service (deploy/docker-compose.yaml) and template-fed to the
# engine base_url/model overrides (`HD_AI_BASE_URL` -> .env.AI_BASE_URL,
# `HD_AI_MODEL` -> .env.AI_MODEL). Defaults match bootstrap/engines.yaml.
# HD_AI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# HD_AI_MODEL=gpt-5.4-mini

# --- Daemon API session tokens (optional) ---
# JWT signing key used by the API service to mint principal session tokens.
# Read directly by the api process (os.Getenv). auth-simple bearer-token auth
# works without it; set a strong random value (openssl rand -hex 32) if you
# want session-token rotation on successful logins.
# For strict "secrets in Vault" compliance, do NOT put the raw value here;
# instead set an hd-lookup: reference that the HD_SECURE_LOADER resolves from
# Vault before the api process reads it:
#   HD_JWT_SIGNING_KEY=hd-lookup:vault:/secrets/data/<ns>/daemon#hd_jwt_signing_key
# (seed the corresponding hd_jwt_signing_key field under that Vault path)
# HD_JWT_SIGNING_KEY=

# --- Bare local daemon (not docker-compose) template settings ---
# These feed `{% .env.X %}` templates and therefore need the HD_ prefix. In
# the compose deployment HD_AI_BASE_URL / HD_AI_MODEL are wired into the
# daemon service (see the "AI provider (start.sh)" section above) and the
# redis settings below are inert: LOCALREDIS redirects all redis-backed core
# drivers, and the AI engine api_key is Vault-only.
# HD_VALKEY_ADDR=127.0.0.1:6379
# HD_VALKEY_PASSWORD=

# --- Vault (daemon side) ---
# Do NOT set operational Vault values here. In the compose deployment the
# daemon receives VAULT_ADDR plus AppRole role_id/secret_id automatically.
# Never set VAULT_K8S_ROLE (kubernetes auth preempts AppRole). For a bare
# local daemon, export VAULT_ADDR / VAULT_ROLE_ID / VAULT_SECRET_ID directly.

# --- Vault container (vault service) ---
# NEVER set VAULT_DEV_ROOT_TOKEN_ID or VAULT_DEV_LISTEN_ADDRESS: the official
# image entrypoint injects them into `vault server` whenever the subcommand is
# "server", so they would take effect if dev mode were ever activated. The
# vault service in this compose deployment is non-dev and needs neither.

# --- Configcheck (make check-config) ---
# CHECK_REMOTE=1
